{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Green Windows sweep (cluster A4, session 3d705fec): run 44606030731, `sweep (windows)` job 135849846469, main at a28027d5ec7dcf6bfe286cde926c4ba13ad16672, concluded `success` (20,269 passed, 872 skipped, 0 failed, 2026-11-19 PST). It runs with only `openssh-key-acl.args` and `unclassified.args` deselected.\n- All 143 lines removed from `posix-shell.args` (136 in 7e0eaf4cd1f, 7 in f163c9c987f) and the 21 shell-stub lines moved out of `path-separators.args` ran. None is in an active deselect file and none failed, so each passed or skipped on its capability guard. The job uses `-q` and prints no per-test skip reasons.\n- Linux `requires_posix_shell` criterion: `requires_posix_shell` is the single module-level `skipif(not os.access('/bin/sh', os.X_OK))` in `tests/_sandbox_capabilities.py`. `tests/test_sandbox_capabilities_posix_shell.py::test_the_mark_does_not_skip_where_bin_sh_exists` asserts its condition is False on any host with `/bin/sh`. It passed in this run's ubuntu-latest jobs (py3.11 135849846512, py3.12 135849846990, py3.13 135849846983), so on Linux no test can skip with that reason. This is evidence by construction plus that test, not a literal `pytest -rs` listing; no CI job prints `-rs`.\nRoot cause is in the earlier comments. Closing as env_integration."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795124724011829001,"uuid":"feb66da2-cf48-47ce-9791-b2dd05deab77"}